      Code="float density=pow(saturate(Texture2DSample(P8,P8Sampler,(P0*float2(P1,P2)+P3*float2(P4,P5)+float2(P6,P7))).r),P9); float main=density*P10;\nfloat sub=pow(saturate(Texture2DSample(P17,P17Sampler,(P0*float2(P11,P12)+P3*float2(P13,P14)+float2(P15,P16))).r),P18)*P19;\nfloat grad=pow(saturate(Texture2DSample(P20,P20Sampler,P0).r),P21)*P22;\nfloat opacity=density*(1.0-saturate(P23))*saturate(grad)*saturate(P24.a);\nfloat3 color=(main*P25.rgb*P26+sub*P27.rgb)*P28*P24.rgb; return float4(color,opacity);"
      OutputType=CMOT_Float4
      Description="Separate normalized source Main_tex R density from source emission gain; source DP Dissolve0..1 consumed as complement lifetime envelope rather than subtraction threshold. Previous normalized threshold candidate nearly suppressed low-valued grunge in actual RHI. This fade topology is explicit recovery adapter inference, original noise shader wiring unavailable. Existing Main_tex_str source child3 affects RGB as before; particle alpha source max1.5 remains stored but bounded before opacity multiply; source curve unchanged; original Gra_tex R/DP Dissolve and pointcolor_str already wired and preserved. Shader wiring is recovery inference; source shader graph unknown. No new numeric tuning, no source scalars/colors/UV/PS/children changed."
